-- title:
--   Special-fibre chart identifications of the Igusa scheme, compatible on overlaps
-- statement:
--   Fix $N \ge 1$ and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $\ell$ in the sense that $\ell$ is a non-unit of $A$, whose residue field $\kappa =$ `ResidueField` $A$ is algebraically closed of characteristic $\ell$. Let $\rho$ be a ring homomorphism from $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)} =$ [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) $\ell$ (the rationals with denominator coprime to $\ell$) to $A$ whose composite with the inclusion $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is the structure map, and give $\kappa$ the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-algebra structure obtained from $\rho$ followed by the residue map. Write $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldFull` $N \subseteq \mathbb{Q}((q))$, $j =$ `jFull` $N$ its element $jq$, and $L =$ `modularFunctionFieldFullC` $\kappa\,N \subseteq \kappa((q))$, with $\tilde\jmath \in L$ the element `jqModC` $\kappa$. The assertion is that there exist $\kappa$-algebra isomorphisms $e_{\mathrm{fin}} \colon \kappa \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}}$ `chartAlgFin` $N\,\ell \to$ `CurveModel.chartRing` $\kappa\,\{\tilde\jmath\}$ and $e_{\infty} \colon \kappa \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}}$ `chartAlgInf` $N\,\ell \to$ `CurveModel.chartRing` $\kappa\,\{\tilde\jmath^{-1}\}$ — here `chartAlgFin` $N\,\ell$ and `chartAlgInf` $N\,\ell$ are the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-subalgebras `chartAlg` $N\,\ell$ of $F$ attached to $\{j\}$ and to $\{j^{-1}\}$, and `CurveModel.chartRing` $\kappa\,S$ consists of the elements of $L$ integral over the $\kappa$-subalgebra generated by $S$ — such that: $e_{\mathrm{fin}}(1 \otimes$ `jChartFin` $N\,\ell) = \tilde\jmath$ and $e_{\infty}(1 \otimes$ `jInvChartInf` $N\,\ell) = \tilde\jmath^{-1}$; every $b \in$ `chartAlgFin` $N\,\ell$ whose underlying Laurent series is `jqN` $N$ has $e_{\mathrm{fin}}(1 \otimes b)$ with Laurent series `jqNModC` $\kappa\,N$; every $b' \in$ `chartAlgInf` $N\,\ell$ whose Laurent series is `jqN` $N \cdot jq^{-N}$ has $e_{\infty}(1 \otimes b')$ with Laurent series `jqNModC` $\kappa\,N \cdot \tilde\jmath^{-N}$; and for all $b \in$ `chartAlgFin` $N\,\ell$, $b' \in$ `chartAlgInf` $N\,\ell$ and $n \in \mathbb{N}$ with $b = b' j^{n}$ in $F$ one has $e_{\mathrm{fin}}(1 \otimes b) = e_{\infty}(1 \otimes b')\,\tilde\jmath^{\,n}$ in $L$.
--
--   This identifies the two affine charts of the special fibre of the Igusa model of $X_0(N)$ over $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ with the corresponding charts of the curve built from the characteristic-$\ell$ modular function field, the last clause being precisely the agreement of the two identifications over the middle chart where $j$ is invertible. It is obtained from [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.exists_algEquiv_residueField_tensor_chartAlg_chartRing_apply_tmul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.exists_algEquiv_residueField_tensor_chartAlg_chartRing_apply_tmul) together with [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.exists_fibreModel_cuspChart_of_chartAlg_of_lift`](thm.html#ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.exists_fibreModel_cuspChart_of_chartAlg_of_lift), and is used by [`ModularCurve.DRLevel.exists_curveModel_iso_fibre0_chartPin_residueField`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRLevel.exists_curveModel_iso_fibre0_chartPin_residueField) to glue the two charts into an isomorphism of the special fibre with a two-chart model.
